---

## What is NOT included in this repository

| Asset type | In this repo? | Notes |
|------------|---------------|-------|
| AD track audio files | No | Not redistributed. You must source or produce your own audio description content. |
| Reference audio (movie/TV soundtracks) | No | Copyrighted by the original rights holders. Not redistributed. |
| Fingerprint hash databases | No | Generated from reference audio. You must generate your own from content you have rights to. |
| Poster images / stills | No | Copyrighted by the original rights holders. Not redistributed. |
| Title metadata (real titles, actors, etc.) | No | Use the admin portal to manage your own catalogue. |

---

## Your responsibilities when deploying DescribeAT

If you deploy DescribeAT, you are responsible for:

1. **Sourcing audio description content** — either producing your own AD tracks or licensing them from content providers under whatever licenses apply in your jurisdiction.
2. **Complying with copyright law** — audio description tracks are derivative works of the original content. Ensure you have the legal right to produce and distribute AD tracks for the content you describe.
3. **Generating your own fingerprint database** — the acoustic fingerprinting engine requires a reference database. You must build this from audio content you have the rights to use.
4. **Hosting your own media** — all media content must be hosted on your own infrastructure (S3, CDN, etc.). No media is distributed with this codebase.

